  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "With a **circular** array `nums`, find the **largest** absolute difference between adjacent elements.\n\n**Note**: In a circular array, the first and last elements are adjacent.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n**Input:** nums = [1,2,4]\n\n**Output:** 3\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nBecause `nums` is circular, `nums[0]` and `nums[2]` are adjacent. They have the largest absolute difference of `|4 - 1| = 3`.\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n**Input:** nums = [-5,-10,-5]\n\n**Output:** 5\n\n**Explanation:**\n\nThe adjacent elements `nums[0]` and `nums[1]` have the largest absolute difference of `|-5 - (-10)| = 5`.\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n* `2 <= nums.length <= 100`\n* `-100 <= nums[i] <= 100`",
    "constraints": [
      "None"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Single line: JSON array of all arguments, e.g. [arg1, arg2, ...]",
    "outputFormat": "Single line: JSON-serialised return value",
